job_description:
About the job

Avensys is a reputed global IT professional services company headquartered in Singapore. Our service spectrum includes enterprise solution consulting, business intelligence, business process automation and managed services. Given our decade of success we have evolved to become one of the top trusted providers in Singapore and service a client base across banking and financial services, insurance, information technology, healthcare, retail and supply chain.




We are hiring skilled Salesforce (Core) Developer responsible for designing, building, and maintaining RPA and PowerApps solutions within Digital Finance, combining low-code expertise with strong software development principles to drive efficient and scalable automation. More details as below:




Job Summary:

A hands-on Salesforce Developer role focused on designing, building, testing, and deploying scalable enterprise solutions by translating business requirements into high-quality technical implementations while collaborating with global teams and contributing to complex, high-impact projects




Role: Salesforce (Core) Developer (Contract)

Contract Start: 1 Year




Job Requirements:

• Must have experience developing on the Salesforce Lightning Platform;

• Solid understanding of Salesforce data modeling, automation tools (Flows, validation rules), and security model;

• Experience building custom business logic using Apex, including triggers, batch jobs, and schedulers;

• Experience developing Lightning Web Components (LWC) and integrating with Apex controllers;

• Exposure to system integrations with Salesforce using REST/SOAP APIs and external services;

• Understanding of Salesforce development lifecycle, including source control, CI/CD, and deployment best practices;

• Ability to work directly with stakeholders to clarify requirements and propose technical solutions;

• Experience working in Agile delivery teams and contributing to sprint planning, estimation, and retrospectives;

• Strong problem solving skills with attention to code quality, performance, and maintainability;

• Demonstrated commitment to teamwork, collaboration, and continuous learning.




Desired Skills:

• Salesforce Certified Platform Developer I (required);

• Salesforce Certified Administrator or Platform App Builder (preferred);

• Salesforce Certified Platform Developer II (a strong plus);

• Additional certifications such as Sales Cloud Consultant or Service Cloud Consultant are an advantage.




Job Responsibilities:

• Designing, developing, testing, and deploying Salesforce solutions using Apex, Lightning Web Components (LWC), Flows, and declarative configurations;

• Translating functional and technical requirements into maintainable, scalable Salesforce solutions;

• Implementing core Salesforce features across Sales Cloud, Service Cloud, and custom objects;

• Developing integrations with external systems using REST/SOAP APIs, Platform Events, and asynchronous processing;

• Applying Salesforce security best practices, including profiles, permission sets, sharing rules, and role hierarchy;

• Writing clean, reusable, and well-documented code following Salesforce and object oriented programming best practices;

• Supporting SIT, UAT, deployment, and post go live stabilization (hypercare);

• Identifying technical risks, performance considerations, and proposing appropriate solutions;

• Collaborating with Technical Architects, Business Analysts, and Project Managers to deliver end to end solutions;

• Contributing to technical documentation such as technical designs, configuration workbooks, and deployment notes;

• Coaching junior developers and contributing to team knowledge sharing and continuous improvement.




If you are interested kindly share you latest resume.




WHAT’S ON OFFER:




You will be remunerated with an excellent base salary and entitled to attractive company benefits. Additionally, you will get the opportunity to enjoy a fun and collaborative work environment, alongside a strong career progression




To submit your application, please apply online or email your UPDATED CV in Microsoft Word format to Shilpi.Gupta@aven-sys.com Your interest will be treated with strict confidentiality.




CONSULTANT DETAILS:

Consultant Name : Shilpi Gupta

Avensys Consulting Pte Ltd

EA Licence 12C5759




Privacy Statement: Data collected will be used for recruitment purposes only. Personal data provided will be used strictly in accordance with the relevant data protection law and Avensys' privacy policy.
